u have to  develop together with sounds together  with minerals you have to develop  another side of your personality it's  about when you when it comes to language  learning it's not about having other  languages under your  it's about being richer being more than  you would be only with one language that  is one thing I fortunately or  unfortunately there are some other  things that depend strictly on  circumstances for example what is  happening right now with me is that my  polish is getting stronger in terms of  in terms of retrieval than a Russian  Russian is stronger in terms of storage  there's this amazing book which is here  so it's called the surprising truth  about how we learn by Benedict Kari and  the author talks about the fact that and  disciplines to language learning as well  you have a capacity of retrieval and  capacity of storage meaning that for  example we store things and then our  capacity of retrieving these things  these pieces of information from memory  depends basically on use so my Russian  is without a doubt stronger in terms of  storage information than my polish but  right now I'm using polish so much for  personal reasons every day that every  time that I want to say something in  Russian polish takes over so to say so  in order to avoid that what you should  do and the reason why actually this is  happening is because I'm using Polish so  much more than the Russian these days  but there is a very easy remedy to that  and the easiest remedy is just to use  both languages at the same time even if  you use one every day for your life  circumstances make you make sure that  you don't forget the other one if I  dedicate or started dedicating 20-30  minutes of Russian everyday the  situation would would get better in no  time  another situation that I've seen and  that happens quite a lot maybe it  happened to you as well is that you  learn a language well because maybe you  spent some time and if in in a country  let's suppose that you're an American  who lived in Spain for three years  learned Spanish to fluency and then all  of a sudden you go and move to another  country  in which people speak a language that is  similar to the one you learnt for  example say a tie and you move to  beautiful Italy and you start speaking  Italian every day then it will happen  again that every time that you want to  speak Spanish Italian will come to the  fore so to say and that happens because  of the retrieval and storage problem  that we have once again easy solution is  just to try to use both if you're in  Italy you will obviously learn and speak  Italian much more so you can actually  organize your time so that you you  actually spend time speaking Spanish  with friends in a bar or reading or  whatever it is the secret is simple just  do a little bit of both languages or  three languages or more every single day  obviously this problem gets bigger and  bigger the more languages you speak so  in order at let's let's recap the first  thing the reason why as a polyglot we're  a hyperpolyglot wherever you want to  call me I don't have I don't struggle  that much with confusing languages is  because I have developed a certain  personality that is not just a result of  the books that I've read or the the  grammar rules that I've started or the  sounds that I have acquired but it's an  overall experience of being richer  because I've integrated faces  experiences colors emotions together  with sounds and grammar rules and words  and the second thing is that there are  some conflicts and sometimes you can  confuse languages due to life  circumstances you you know it's never  always the same thing when it comes to  languages because you're suitable life  situation changes so in that case make  sure that if you're using one language  more than the other just make sure that  you start using somehow passively and/or  actively the other language that is  being less dominant in that precise  moment otherwise you will r